course: dictionary
lesson: 13787
title: Going where you are not wanted
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To intrude is to go into a place, or join in with a group, when you are not wanted or not invited. Think of walking into a room that is not yours without knocking.
explain: Intrude is often used to be polite. «Sorry to intrude, but may I ask a question?» The speaker knows they might not be welcome, so they say sorry first.
explain: Intrude can also mean to disturb or spoil something. «The loud drill intruded on our quiet picnic.» The drill did not walk into the picnic, but it spoiled the peace.
explain: An intruder is someone who enters a home or school without permission. When you read intrude, look for clues about who is not welcome and what boundary is being crossed.
fact: Intrude is a verb: intrude, intrudes, intruded, intruding.
fact: «Intrude» means to go into a place or join in when you are not wanted or not invited.
fact: «Intrude on» means to disturb or spoil something, such as peace or quiet.
fact: «Intruder» means a person who enters a place without permission.
fact: Polite phrases like «Sorry to intrude» show that the speaker knows they might be unwelcome.
exercise: «The loud dog intruded on our quiet picnic.» What does intruded on mean here? | Tidied up | Cooked for | *Disturbed and spoiled | Ran away from
exercise: «Sorry to intrude, but may I join you?» Why does the speaker say sorry first? | They have lost their bag | They have won a prize | *They might not be wanted there | They are very hungry
exercise: «The stranger climbed in through the back window of the house.» Find and copy one word that means a person who enters without permission. | house | climbed | window | *stranger
test: «The stranger tried to enter the house without permission.» Which word means someone who gets into a place without permission? | *Intruder | Neighbour | Helper | Guest
test: What does intrude mean? | To sleep soundly | *To go where you are not wanted | To invite someone in warmly | To clean a room
exam: Mia's brother walked into her den without knocking, and she said, «You intruded on my private space.» What does intruded mean here? | Painted | Helped | Hid | *Went into a place where he was not wanted
